{"id": "EUVD-2026-82241", "enisaUuid": "3e8e8396-4c51-3c2b-ad2d-3c8d31d6498e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nACPI: RISC-V: Check acpi_get_handle() status in riscv_acpi_add_prt_dep()\n\nIn riscv_acpi_add_prt_dep(), the acpi_get_handle() call can fail which\nwould leave link_handle uninitialized.\n\nFix it by checking the acpi_get_handle() return status and skip the entry\nif it fails.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:11:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:06:06", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f8625752bfdf108a0000116aa583b3efe767b540", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4cdcf4e19ed3127afd787f026d4ec56ae4d2a4ed", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/088c1c85921344d7244ca2e8d5d336ae7461de6e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/20435bda13f1219891ed0ce41207e320a916ff9c"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93133", "GHSA-6x8h-vjg9-qvc5"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2ac9ecb2-6f2a-3c6f-95bb-ef60190aca79", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1b173cc4bfcdcf4a49927952ba3a445c5b293723 <f8625752bfdf108a0000116aa583b3efe767b540"}, {"id": "6a645a14-1cec-378c-84a1-765ce98261ce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1b173cc4bfcdcf4a49927952ba3a445c5b293723 <20435bda13f1219891ed0ce41207e320a916ff9c"}, {"id": "7feb9f97-3ad3-3ad6-b8de-daa2bd06190a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12"}, {"id": "88fc215c-1553-38e6-8ae1-533007677633", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "9070d7b5-0de8-360f-8945-fb703acc4583", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "b82c6b56-59b1-3d24-8343-c615adc4791f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "e131607e-0667-3ae7-9ff2-09c6c1356fc